  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the child as if embodying the text's message",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the severely malnourished child, interpreting the child as 'just trying to do my part' — a deictic projection that frames the viewer as the actor performing the action described in the text. This projection is implicit, not explicit, but it is strongly implied by the meme's structure: the viewer is invited to identify with the child's suffering while simultaneously being told the child is 'doing their part,' which creates a false equivalence and moralizing of suffering. The user is not directly addressed with 'you' or 'me,' but the framing of the child as a passive participant in a larger system implicitly positions the viewer as the one who must 'do their part' — thus projecting the user's identity onto the child's role.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
